      <p class="note"><a href="/guides.html">Guides</a> / Units</p>
      <h1>Metric and Imperial Conversions Explained</h1>
      <p class="lead">Most of the world uses metric units. The United States and a few other countries still use imperial units for everyday measurements. Knowing the exact conversion factors saves guesswork when you travel, shop online or follow a recipe.</p>

      <h2>Length</h2>
      <p>The key figure is that one inch is exactly 2.54 centimetres. Everything else follows from that:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>1 foot = 12 inches = 30.48 cm</li>
        <li>1 yard = 3 feet = 0.9144 m</li>
        <li>1 mile = 1,760 yards = 1.609344 km</li>
      </ul>
      <p>A quick estimate: 1 mile is roughly 1.6 km, and 1 km is roughly 0.62 miles.</p>

      <h2>Weight</h2>
      <p>One pound is exactly 0.45359237 kilograms, and one ounce is one sixteenth of a pound. A stone, used mostly for body weight in the UK, is 14 pounds, or about 6.35 kg.</p>
      <p>For quick estimates, 1 kg is about 2.2 pounds. A 70 kg person weighs about 154 pounds.</p>

      <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>

      <h2>Temperature</h2>
      <p>Temperature does not scale in a straight line like length or weight, so it needs a formula:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Celsius to Fahrenheit: multiply by 9/5, then add 32.</li>
        <li>Fahrenheit to Celsius: subtract 32, then multiply by 5/9.</li>
        <li>Celsius to Kelvin: add 273.15.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Water freezes at 0 °C, which is 32 °F, and boils at 100 °C, which is 212 °F. For an oven or a fever, these formulas are the ones to use.</p>

      <h2>Try it yourself</h2>
      <p>The <a href="../tools/unit-converter.html">Unit Converter</a> handles length, weight and temperature. Type a value in either box and the other one updates.</p>
      <section class="worked">
        <h2>Worked example</h2>
        <p>A height of 5 feet 7 inches is 67 inches. Multiply by 2.54 centimetres per inch: 67 × 2.54 = 170.2 cm. A temperature of 100 °F is (100 − 32) × 5 ÷ 9 = 37.8 °C.</p>
      </section>
